   "title": "Typical application",
   "page": 9,
   "description": "An inverter without a Schmitt input has about 2.2 MΩ from its output back to its input, about 32 pF from each of those two nodes to ground, and 16 pF between the two nodes. Its output feeds one Schmitt-trigger channel of the SN74LVC2G14, which drives a 50 pF load. The second channel is idle.",
   "parts": [
